  <paragraphs xml:id="description">
    <title>Course Description</title>
    <p>
      The development of selected mathematical concepts will be traced from ancient Babylon. The course will focus on mathematical creation as a human endeavor done within a cultural context.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="instructional-format">
    <title>Instructional Format</title>
    <p>This is a face-to-face course, which means we will meet in person.</p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="course-materials">
    <title>Course Materials</title>
    <p>
      We will use a variety of sources for this class. All of them will be either posted on Canvas, or are available electronically through the library.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="office-hours">
    <title>Student Office Hours</title>
    <p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          <em>Erich McAlister's Office Hours:</em> MW 1-2:30pm in EBH 262, F 1-2:30pm in the PEC
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="feedback">
    <title>Feedback and Communication</title>
    <p>
      Communication of all course information will occur via Canvas as well as in class. Most assignments will be submitted and graded online in Canvas.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="missing-class">
    <!--Course policies are made by intructional teams; these are examples.-->
    <title>Missing Class</title>
    <p>
      Class attendance is expected every day. This class requires active participation; your presence in class affects both your and your classmates' understanding of the material. 
    </p>
    <p>
      If you need to miss class for an extended period of time, let your professor know so that we may work out a remote accommodation.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>

  <paragraphs xml:id="tech">
    <title>Technology and Software Requirements</title>
    <p>
      You will need to be able to access Canvas to submit assignments online. Internet access and a scanning device are required. Calculators may be occassionally useful.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
</section>
